# UI kit exports (OpenSekai editor)

`@oshi-connect/ui` does **not** export `Checkbox`. Do not invent kit components.

1. Before `import { X } from '@oshi-connect/ui'`, confirm `X` is in `.local/ui/dist/index.js` (or the kit `dist/index.js` ensure-ui snapshots). If it is missing, do not import it.
2. Editor boolean fields use the existing native pattern — not a kit `Checkbox`:

```svelte
<label class="visibility-control">
  <input type="checkbox" checked={value} disabled={off} onchange={...} />
  Label
</label>
```

Same pattern as Visible, Autofocus, Affect, and related Inspector fields. Use `settleCheckbox` when a failed reply must restore the prior value.
3. Principle: use the kit **only when it already exports the control**. Do not assume a name exists because another product or a prior chat mentioned it.
